{
  "id": "ss.relic.card-splinter",
  "name": "Splinter",
  "description": "One wing-blade snapped across its middle: the two halves still carry the blade's own vocabulary — bone frame, grey membrane, the bone spine down one edge and the cold cutting edge down the other, a vein across each — and they lean apart into a V with the break at the right and five chips of frame and membrane flying out of it. The relic breaks a spent spine into two splinters that fly on, and a break still shedding its chips is the moment that says so. `ss.proj.card` is not composed directly because a document cannot be cut in half; the shards are redrawn from its parts at its size, and the jagged edges are where the two drawings agree they were once one. It stays off ss.relic.card by being one blade in pieces instead of three whole.",
